{"title":"MIE 2015","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_1_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_2_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_3_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_4_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_5_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_6_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_7_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given any three sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. The set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82a0a0f362fe582d8435fe9b6870ffab4c4e971d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G-H$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to the set:\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/776d12716c144863172a143b775e840dfb66e5ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(G\\cup F)-(F-H)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d14dc9407f7985cfcc32512da1ecde1ceea7f1f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(G\\cup H)-(H-F)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1cb05edc1d7b66644ed65f62945e0543ee7c01d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(G\\cup(H-F))\\cap\\overline{H}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc732fc362fbceb8957e140eea8e9acef2122ae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{G}\\cup(H\\cap F)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/d/96d4a217251ad914d2012cd9ff349f711180f0d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\overline{H}\\cap G)\\cap(G-F)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77e3d4c4c56d4a72b0a21f50f613a6474503109e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+ax^2+bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"16\" /> has real roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b06ce2c64dc6eacae94af2f2783e199e3b5bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\alpha$\" width=\"25\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d971c19d77fc0a91046a2b68b7147a4097acc1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\alpha}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"14\" height=\"37\" />. Thus the value of the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/3507b0f5d29f3c52b7974d4590b2d0d37a77ad73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c^2+ac+\\frac{b}{c^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"125\" height=\"37\" /> is:\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015/Day_1/Problem_2\" title=\"MIE 2015/Day 1/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19d89395691277353566633f4adaa46ec6559177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^m+14400=n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" />. Find the remainder of the division of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Compute\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/4/fe4214baf19eaf97f08ef69b9eb3a314777761e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"25\" height=\"50\" /> Img<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea11308bc75f828a41aa89c27ba34bb8a230ca65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\right.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"6\" height=\"18\" />cis<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e36c80391e4324ebec93324096a5832daea608af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left.^{2k-1}\\frac{\\pi}{36}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e375d3908ef490e54971dae67a3219af5561b6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2+\\sqrt3}{4\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{36}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"58\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e690e3f621de7db49fcf88e2a5d6b9d7095801bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2-\\sqrt3}{4\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{36}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"58\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b3974d8820877b8a6d117ba87a2a94c7fb0b4e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{36}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"57\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/c/abc735e1bd89ec79529573a84fa47de18b46a3bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Note: Img(w) is the imaginary part of w.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a6978d4a2f0ceaad836d2179741a80d52e6b15db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=x^2+ax+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"21\" />. It's known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b288d97b04c09c660abf5f2a72f105ebce56aa0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(P(P(x)))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> have a root in common. Therefore, we can say that for every value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7a561a4dca209670f8e51f6d3a9a17a31834cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(-1)P(1)&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f2492a10c661f1697bda5a0695f42b0c944178d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(-1)P(1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3cc63068f93595081d2c8688ffe0a5b92079116c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(-1)+P(1)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf72fbbb0094e38a80babca62ddccc4b07cbfa85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(0)P(1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a3fab53ea44987e595819c2a09a0c147532231.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(0)+P(1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> be a geometric progression and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/6965c319edede591a94ec7fad32c7f044e93a8ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log\\left(\\frac{5c}{a}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"70\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e816f25c4943b05cb8d12efe51c7f0c64040a16d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log\\left(\\frac{3b}{5c}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"70\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51a592f1d3077258ece543a373c2ef4ef6e3d7bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log\\left(\\frac{a}{3b}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"33\" /> be a arithmetic progression, both in these order, so we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p>(a) are the sides of a obtusangle triangle.\n</p><p>(b) are the sides of a acutangle triangle that's not equilateral.\n</p><p>(c) are the sides of a equilateral triangle.\n</p><p>(d) are the sides of a right triangle.\n</p><p>(e) can't be the sides of a triangle.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015/Day_1/Problem_6\" title=\"MIE 2015/Day 1/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Compute\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/9253258c27873aaa5304ed47bcd90cae3df250c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2016}{5}+\\binom{2017}{5}+\\binom{2018}{5}+\\binom{2019}{5}+\\binom{2020}{5}+\\binom{2016}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"494\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><br />\n(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e86a873187b4cbf62608125338940a20db2fd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2020}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"66\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><br />\n(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b84fde81acc2900601fa45d96fa557b45dfe4262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2020}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"60\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><br />\n(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/1/7a1b7f5712f5338bf4415a2481dfae7cb354be9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2021}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"60\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><br />\n(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26a82c758d16086d92e61ef4ed1003b9a47e3d94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2021}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"60\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><br />\n(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a646591e983c4f136388f64b6c95a37dcd35ceec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2022}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"66\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015/Day_1/Problem_7\" title=\"MIE 2015/Day 1/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1_2\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The ingeters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf94913c706906b077c35767802b46872983d829.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,a_3,...,a_{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"11\" /> are in arithmetic progression of ratio not equal to zero. The sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/5/115bb1b8c0ebd40df816d2b3c09bca3f0cf61701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,a_2,a_{10})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/c/62c386bc38044b50a06e5b4e682f5ef70e4ab2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_6,a_j,a_{25})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> are both in geometric progression. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc19ca9685e2dcc4316b6dda7d448dad7254d724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/4109b30add027513875f41cb77905d7017c7c066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\{0,1,2,3,...\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/65657dc7570cd3c4156b1068190a86773ea96f4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_0(x)=\\frac{1}{1-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08be4b5dc9e15eb66766beaefc63c64806cf0fa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_n(x)=f_0(f_{n-1}(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />, for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28324eb1d52d541982598613d2d7ac4cb4e526e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b03e04be626dff50086a7c05d3bc3417193b2086.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{2016}(2016)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015/Day_2/Problem_2\" title=\"MIE 2015/Day 2/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3_2\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> be a complex number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da748614538ce0b09809091f80828ae9dd16efd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2Z}{\\overline{Z}i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"25\" height=\"39\" /> has an argument <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b953d396f434900925523b4e79b2ff52346e40a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa1f65a620f7a3050d9af651d1cb815d3f09b88e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3\\pi}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/525636b9fd4cf39e5bb9fdad23cb67b30437510f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_3(2Z+2\\overline{Z}+1)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"20\" />. Find the complex number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4_2\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> as the matrix 2016 x 2016, such that its elements satisfy the equality:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3e4418421866149f4544f1c4f482a72a23dacfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i,j}=\\begin{pmatrix}i+j-2\\\\j-1\\end{pmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"140\" height=\"43\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb19d02f2652f11d42f7efe76d637401d650724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j\\in\\{1,2,...,2016\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Compute det(A).\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5_2\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find the solution of the equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5ddad67792e924132f455d118c25d953c43abbdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x\\left(1+\\tan x\\tan\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=4-\\cot x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"270\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6_2\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/008b003e1a375158d08c787b5471e95fefbfcdb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-7m^2=(5m-2n)^2+49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"226\" height=\"19\" />. Find all the pairs of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca10ffe3531cf1faf6222be7eac407c47bef878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> that satisfy this equation.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7_2\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Three player sits around a table and play, alternatively, a dice of six faces. The first player throw the dice, then the player at its left plays, and then it goes, until the finish of the game. The one that throw the dice and get the side with number 6, wins the game and it ends. If a player gets the number 1, he loses its chance and the player at its right will throw the dice. The game will continue until someone gets the number 6. What's the probability of the first player to throw the dice to win?\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The equation of the circumference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7b482e55316f03452a98716845c3bd890a6450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> be a circumference of radius 1 wich moves internally tangentiating the circumference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, without slipping between the points of contact, in other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> internally rolls on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:MIE_2015_day_1_problem_8.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/47/MIE_2015_day_1_problem_8.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"645\" height=\"261\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><br />\nLet the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> such that in the beginning of the movement of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is at the tangent point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86f58cb609fa753024f1173510c877971f8e4e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, like in the figure a. After some movement, the angle between the X axis and the line between the centers of the circumferences is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Find the coordinates of the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> marked on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Find the equation of the cartesian coordinates of the geometric place of the point P when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> varies in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa914ed4bd30af60a82d993a58fafc8144fdf3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,2\\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />.</li></ul>\n<p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015/Day_2/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"MIE 2015/Day 2/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A chord intersects the diameter of a circle of center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> according to an angle of 45°. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the extreme points of this chord, and the distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2d3fcc93e75c0e9b61822ff041467f47f9c5bfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC&#39;$\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a13a33e3fb93f9b62f1267bc703de994dccd7507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt3+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" /> cm. The radius of the circle is 2 cm, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the farther extremity of the diameter from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" />. The extension of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35fcf9255437d760c3e9d87a4c5fc7007f2d8976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BC}{A&#39;}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"31\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015/Day_2/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"MIE 2015/Day 2/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A cone is inscribed into a cube <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055dcba798b1424c44c2606d913e0f2edab1c5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" /> such that the base of the cone is the circle inscribed in the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> of the cube. The vertex of the cone is the center of the opposite face of the cube. The projection of the vertex H on the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> coincides with the vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Compute the area of section of the cone by the surface <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e7ae1949ae0465b07fd76dc2abef1af3203158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABH$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the side of the cube.\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015/Day_2/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"MIE 2015/Day 2/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2015&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018000756\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.077 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.103 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 642/1000000\nPost‐expand include s